# Pressure Sensor Component Guide

## Overview
The pressure sensor component provides weight measurement functionality using HX711 load cell amplifiers. It supports dual sensors for weight distribution detection and includes a comprehensive calibration system.

## Key Files
- [components/pressure_sensor/include/pressure_sensor.hpp](mdc:components/pressure_sensor/include/pressure_sensor.hpp): Implementation of the PressureSensor class methods
- [example.cpp](mdc:components/pressure_sensor/src/example.cpp): Interface example for the pressure sensor class
- [components/pressure_sensor/src/pressure_sensor.cpp](mdc:components/pressure_sensor/src/pressure_sensor.cpp): Contains a sample application for calibration and usage
- External dependency: [managed_components/supcik__hx711/include/hx711.hpp](mdc:managed_components/supcik__hx711/include/hx711.hpp)

## Features
- **Dual Sensor Support**: Two pressure sensors for weight distribution measurement
- **Calibration System**:
  - Zero-point calibration (Tare method)
  - Scale factor calibration using known weights
  - Persistent storage of calibration parameters in NVS
- **Multi-Sample Reading**: Support for noise reduction through multiple sample averaging

## Hardware Configuration
- Uses GPIO pins 15, 16, 47, 21 for interfacing with HX711 chips
- Configured for Channel A with 128 gain
- Default calibration weight: 1kg standard weight

## Calibration Workflow
1. Zero-point calibration (empty scale)
2. Scale factor calibration (with known weight)
3. Storage of calibration parameters to NVS
4. Continuous measurement mode
